>
>
> First of all, it /is/ a pause, so that's what I'm calling it. It is the
> textual representation of a mandatory pause in a Lojban speech stream.
>

I mean, seriously, why do you think the Lojban name of '.' is DENPA bu?
"denpa bu" in English is "pause character".

